MEMORANDUM OF UNDERSTANDING BETWEEN
LARAMIE COUNTY SCHOOL DISTRICT NUMBER ONE AND
THE CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING
Parties.This Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) is made and entered into by and
between Laramie County School District Number 1(District), whose address is 2810
House Avenue, Cheyenne, WY 82001, and the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming,(City),
through the Cheyenne Police Department, whose address is 415 West 18th Street,
Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001.
2.
Purpose.The purpose of this MOU is to delineate the terms in which the City will
provide police services to the District schools within the recognized area of jurisdiction
of the City and for school-related events during the academic year, including summer
school of each year(Academic Year), under the School Resource Officer(s)Program
(SRO).The primary charge of the SRO Program is the reduction, prevention, and
responsiveness to school-related violence and crime.The SRO Program creates and
maintains a safe, secure, and crime-free learning environment for students, educators
and the District. In addition, the SRO Program is designed to develop and enhance
rapport between youth, parents, the surrounding school community, police officers,
school leaders, and staff.
3.
Term of MOU. This MOU shall commence upon the day and date last signed and
executed by the duly authorized representatives of the parties to this MOU and shall
remain in full force and effect until August 31, 2026. This MOU shall specifically
supersede any prior MOU entered into by the Parties and in effect at the
commencement of thisMOU.
4
Payment._The District agrees to pay the City for the services described herein.
Specifically, the District shall pay as follows:
A.
All costs of salary and benefits incurred by the City in the performance of
duties under this Agreement shall be paid by the City, and the District shall
reimburse the Cityfor all such costs.
B.
Said sum shall be invoiced to the District monthly and in arrears.
C.
The Citywill provide cellular phones for use in official communications with
District employees.The phones shall remain the property of the City.The
service plan. The City agrees to be responsible for the cost of the phones
themselves, including any related hardware, as well as maintenance,
upgrades, and replacements.
Memorandum of Understanding School Resourcc Officers Program
