6.
Responsibilities of the City.
A.
The City agrees to provide the District with seven (7) SROs and one SRO
Supervisor for the 2025-2026 Academic Year. The supervisor's
responsibilities will be to manage and coordinate the City's performance
under this Agreement.
B.
The City agrees that SRO duties are to respond to and investigate criminal
acts on District property and/or at District events during normal school hours,
or as otherwise agreed to, during the Academic Year.
C.
The City agrees that the SRO may initiate appropriate law enforcement
actions to address criminal matters, including matters that threaten the safety
and security of the school or its occupants, and/or intervene with staff or
students when necessary to ensure the immediate safety of persons in the
school environment inlight of an actual or imminent threat to health or safety.
Any such intervention shall be reasonably calculated toprotect the physical
safety of members within the school community, while minimizing, to the
extent possible, any unintended negative effects on students. All law
enforccment actions and interventions to protect the safety of others shall be
consistent with all applicable laws, regulations, and policies.
D.
The City agrees that except for felony offenses or criminal offenses that
constitute a threat to the safety of the school or public ("Serious Offenses"),
the SRO will notify and consult with the school principal or his designee prior
to questioning a student.
E.
The City agrees that except for Serious Offenses, the SRO will delay
questioning a student until the parent or guardian arrives.
Memorandum of Understanding School Resource Officers Program
